;; the skill's file broke on my edit: rewrite it whole, with the step this turn added
(define-skill open-osa-pr
  "Open a PR from this box against open-super-agent-remake's shared branch: rebase, run CI's own commands locally (the i18n gate is the one that bites), push with the token in the URL, then let CI speak."
  ;; when-to-use: an ask to get local OSA work onto the shared repo — "tạo PR", "đưa lên nhánh i18n", "team sẽ review rồi merge" — on a branch of one's own, never a push straight to the shared branch
  ;; evidence: 2026-11-11, 53 local commits on top of 12 the team had pushed: rebase was clean because the ranges did not overlap (comm -12 of two name-only diffs was empty), `python -m osa.i18n` exited 1 on 7 backend + 3 frontend strings my own commits had added, and after adding en/vi to the four locale files the gate exited 0; PR #50 then ran backend 12m13s / frontend 13s / docker 34s all pass and came back mergeStateStatus CLEAN. A second, unrelated fix (PR #51: backend 5m39s / frontend / docker green) went through the same path from a separate worktree, in one pass.
  ;; 1. git fetch --prune; the clone may be shallow, so compare against the pre-fetch tip (dac00da..887fd7d) — "887fd7d~12" fails — and check overlap with comm -12 of the two `git diff --name-only` sets.
  ;; 2. git rebase origin/i18n-vi; there is no branch called "i18n" — the shared one is i18n-vi. Rebase works only while the branch is still local: once a branch is pushed and has fallen behind, nodecode-guard refuses `git push --force`, so update it by `git merge origin/i18n-vi` into the branch (resolve, commit) and push normally — `git push --force-with-lease` never runs from a shell on this box. If the branch is already pushed AND its diff no longer differs (the same work went in by another PR), a rebase can come out empty: `git log origin/i18n-vi..origin/BRANCH` then `git diff origin/i18n-vi origin/BRANCH` — empty means close it with a note instead of opening an empty PR.
  ;; 3. Run the CI file's own steps before pushing: compileall + import osa.server; python -m osa.catalog / templates / i18n / skillpacks verify-sources; pytest -q; scripts/run_evals.py --base-ref i18n-vi (the PR gate compares against the target branch's baseline, not the PR's own); in web/: npm test && npm run build (osa/static/dist is gitignored).
  ;; 4. translations: missing keys fail the gate, extra keys only warn; new keys go in osa/locales/{en,vi}.json and web/src/locales/{en,vi}.json, written with json.dump(..., ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) plus a trailing newline, which is the file's shape.
  ;; 5. push: plain `git push origin BRANCH` once the credential chain is sane — a helper `!f() { echo username=x-access-token; echo password=$(cat /home/boxes/.nodecode/gh-token); }; f` for https://github.com, plus an empty helper entry before it to clear the inherited one. If it says "Invalid username or token", do NOT paste a token into the URL yet: a stale `url.*.insteadOf` rewrite in ~/.gitconfig can be sending an hour-old ghs_ token instead (git remote -v prints the rewritten URL), and /opt/devbox-tools/bin/boxes-github-credential quits when the devbox's GitHub integration is disconnected — see memory devbox-github-git-wiring. Fallback that always works: git push "https://x-access-token:$(cat /home/boxes/.nodecode/gh-token)@github.com/VagabondKingsman/open-super-agent-remake.git" BRANCH:BRANCH.
  ;; 6. after any commit made on the checked-out branch, re-run git branch -f <pr-branch> HEAD and push again: a commit made after the branch was created stays behind, and the push answers "Everything up-to-date" while the PR still shows the old head (this happened once here; `git ls-remote ... refs/heads/<branch>` is what told the truth).
  ;; 7. gh pr create --base i18n-vi --head <branch> --body-file ... with GH_TOKEN from that file; the body follows .github/pull_request_template.md (Task / Đã đổi / Verify / Rủi ro), Vietnamese by default, tickboxes only for what actually ran; add one bullet to CHANGELOG.md's [未发布] ### remake section, written in Chinese like the rest of it.
  ;; 8. confirm with gh pr checks <n> (backend is ~12 minutes) and gh pr view --json mergeStateStatus; then leave the checkout on the PR branch and point local i18n-vi at origin/i18n-vi.
  ;; 9. a second, unrelated small fix gets its own worktree off the shared branch — git worktree add /tmp/base origin/i18n-vi, work and test there, push its branch, open its own PR — so the live checkout stays on the code the running service was tested with. One venv serves it (/home/boxes/osa/.venv/bin/python) and web/node_modules is symlinked in; its eval run reports the base branch's scenario count (27), not the big PR's (35).
  ;; 10. after the merge: #50 and #51 were merged by `app/cursor` within minutes, without a human click — read it
  ;;     with gh pr view N --json state,mergedAt,mergedBy rather than waiting for a review signal; then the branch
  ;;     keeps moving (16 more commits within 2.5 h), so the live checkout must follow origin/i18n-vi — skill
  ;;     osa-serve-merged-branch (rebuild web/, restart the osa unit, verify manifest and the bundle hash).
  )
